MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Eagles and the Beach Boys felt like natural next choices because familiar songs in greatest-hits collections fit my repeated interest in older hit compilations.",
    "Carole King and Bread appealed through warm melodies and gentle vocals, connecting with what drew me to Simon & Garfunkel and Melanie."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Earth Wind & Fire's funk and soul felt less suited to my mood than melodic folk-pop and classic rock, even though these are also familiar older hits.",
    "I could not judge The Definitive Collection without knowing the artist; the promise of a collection alone does not make it appealing."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Older greatest-hits collections seemed to be treated as equally appealing, although the sound and voices matter more to me than their era alone.",
    "My interest in rock does not mean every rock album is an immediate choice: Tom Petty and Queen fit parts of my taste, but I would defer them today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My interest in Simon & Garfunkel and Melanie points toward gentle storytelling, clear melodies and warm vocals, which make Carole King especially appealing now.",
    "Something can fit my taste without being something I choose today; Carpenters and Gary Lewis appeal, but I would prioritize only a few albums this visit."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in familiar older songs, but sometimes gave era and compilation format more weight than my current preference for melodic folk-pop and classic rock."
}
